    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d581">

                <pb facs="0803" n="704" xml:id="pg704"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">812.52/2013: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to
                        the Ambassador in Mexico</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                            >Daniels</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1936-10-14T20:00:00-05:00">October 14, 1936—8
                        p.m.</date></dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>176. Your 179, October 11, 6 p.m.,<anchor n="15" xml:id="d581-f1"/> and telegram
                    from Yepis of October 10, 2 p.m. Yepis authorized to proceed Cuidad Obregón for
                    purpose indicated in his telegram. He is being instructed to make it entirely
                    clear that he is acting in an unofficial and personal capacity and that in
                    rendering requested assistance he is not engaging the responsibility of this
                    Government in any way. The Department assumes of course that his cooperation in
                    the matter will be agreeable to all parties concerned.</p>
                <p>Charles C. Gidney, jr., non-career, appointed Vice Consul at Guaymas for
                    temporary duty, proceeding from Washington today. Request provisional
                    recognition. Inform DADO.<anchor n="16" xml:id="d581-f2"/></p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Hull</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
